
====================================================================================================
A. sech envelope widths: the tooth formula sech(2 pi k nu_rep tau) belongs to a FIELD envelope sech(pi t/(2 tau))
====================================================================================================
  field sech(pi t/(2 tau)):  FWHM_field = 1.676803 tau,  FWHM_intensity(sech^2) = 1.122200 tau
  field sech(pi t/tau):      FWHM_field = 0.838401 tau,  FWHM_intensity(sech^2) = 0.561100 tau  (the printed pair)
  FT check (ratio to omega = 0):
    omega tau = 0.5: FT[sech(pi t/2tau)] = 0.886819 vs sech(omega tau) = 0.886819;  FT[sech(pi t/tau)] = 0.969544 vs sech(omega tau/2) = 0.969544
    omega tau = 1.0: FT[sech(pi t/2tau)] = 0.648054 vs sech(omega tau) = 0.648054;  FT[sech(pi t/tau)] = 0.886819 vs sech(omega tau/2) = 0.886819
    omega tau = 2.0: FT[sech(pi t/2tau)] = 0.265802 vs sech(omega tau) = 0.265802;  FT[sech(pi t/tau)] = 0.648054 vs sech(omega tau/2) = 0.648054
    omega tau = 3.0: FT[sech(pi t/2tau)] = 0.099328 vs sech(omega tau) = 0.099328;  FT[sech(pi t/tau)] = 0.425096 vs sech(omega tau/2) = 0.425096
  -> with teeth at omega = 2 pi k nu_rep, sech(2 pi k nu_rep tau) is the transform of sech(pi t/(2 tau)); the
     printed FWHM pair (0.8384, 0.5611) tau describes sech(pi t/tau), whose teeth would read sech(pi k nu_rep tau).

