====================================================================================================
G. Monroe 1995 Lamb-Dicke anchor (9Be+, 313 nm, modes 11.2/18.2/29.8 MHz; quoted eta = 0.21, 0.12, 0.09)
====================================================================================================
   11.2 MHz: x0 = 7.076 nm; eta(|dk| = 2k) = 0.2841, eta(sqrt2 k, 90 deg crossing) = 0.2009, eta(k) = 0.1420; quoted 0.21 -> implied |dk . e|/k = 1.478
   18.2 MHz: x0 = 5.551 nm; eta(|dk| = 2k) = 0.2229, eta(sqrt2 k, 90 deg crossing) = 0.1576, eta(k) = 0.1114; quoted 0.12 -> implied |dk . e|/k = 1.077
   29.8 MHz: x0 = 4.338 nm; eta(|dk| = 2k) = 0.1742, eta(sqrt2 k, 90 deg crossing) = 0.1232, eta(k) = 0.0871; quoted 0.09 -> implied |dk . e|/k = 1.034
  -> the x anchor needs |dk| = sqrt2 k (a 90 degree crossing with dk along x), not 2k; the y and z anchors are
     reproduced to 8% and 3% by a projection k on each axis (a second 90 degree pair whose dk bisects y and z).

====================================================================================================
H. Morigi EIT fixture (Fig. 3: nu = 2.0068, gamma = 20, Omega_1 = Omega_2 = 17 MHz, |Delta| = 70 MHz) in the plan's sign
====================================================================================================
  Omega_r = sqrt(Omega_1^2 + Omega_2^2) = 24.0416 MHz; the EIT resonance condition Omega_r^2 = 4 nu (nu + Delta) gives 578.01 at Delta = +70
  light shift of the bright state (sqrt(Delta^2 + Omega_r^2) - Delta)/2 = 2.0068 MHz = nu -> the fixture sits on resonance only for Delta > 0 in the plan's sign
  Section 4.2.3 closed form: Delta = +70, Omega_r = 24.04 -> 0.005102  ((gamma/4Delta)^2 = 0.005102);  Delta = -70 (the caption's sign read in the plan's convention) -> -1.0051 (negative: trips the A_- - A_+ <= 0 guard);  Delta = +70 with Omega_r = 17 (a single Rabi frequency in place of the quadrature sum) -> 0.1467, 29x the target

====================================================================================================
I. Floquet function under the ADOPTED Mathieu sign d^2x/dxi^2 + [a - 2q cos 2xi] x = 0 (a = 0)
====================================================================================================
  q = 0.1, adopted a - 2q cos      : beta = 0.070850; c_+1/c_0 = -0.023322 (pred -0.023319), c_-1/c_0 = -0.026875 (pred -0.026870); u'(0)/(i beta u(0)) = 1.103585 vs 1 + q = 1.1000
  q = 0.1, RMP-quantum a + 2q cos  : beta = 0.070850; c_+1/c_0 = +0.023322 (pred +0.023319), c_-1/c_0 = +0.026875 (pred +0.026870); u'(0)/(i beta u(0)) = 0.902730 vs 1 - q = 0.9000
  q = 0.2, adopted a - 2q cos      : beta = 0.142551; c_+1/c_0 = -0.043590 (pred -0.043568), c_-1/c_0 = -0.058014 (pred -0.057969); u'(0)/(i beta u(0)) = 1.216548 vs 1 + q = 1.2000
  q = 0.2, RMP-quantum a + 2q cos  : beta = 0.142551; c_+1/c_0 = +0.043590 (pred +0.043568), c_-1/c_0 = +0.058014 (pred +0.057969); u'(0)/(i beta u(0)) = 0.809524 vs 1 - q = 0.8000
  q = 0.3, adopted a - 2q cos      : beta = 0.216059; c_+1/c_0 = -0.061151 (pred -0.061088), c_-1/c_0 = -0.094454 (pred -0.094267); u'(0)/(i beta u(0)) = 1.343415 vs 1 + q = 1.3000
  q = 0.3, RMP-quantum a + 2q cos  : beta = 0.216059; c_+1/c_0 = +0.061151 (pred +0.061088), c_-1/c_0 = +0.094454 (pred +0.094267); u'(0)/(i beta u(0)) = 0.718569 vs 1 - q = 0.7000
  -> under the adopted sign c_{+-1}/c_0 = -q/((2 +- beta)^2 - a): the lowest-order bracket is [1 - (q/2) cos(omega_rf t)] and
     u'(0) = i nu (1 + q) at u(0) = 1; the RMP's quantum section (W(t) with +2q cos) is the opposite rf phase origin,
     [1 + (q/2) cos] and i nu (1 - q). C_0 = 1 + 3q^2/16 is even in q and unaffected (check_c0_floquet.py).

