K. Filter-function infrared cutoff on a 1/omega^4 spectrum: omega_min = 1/T against 2 pi/T (T = 1, omega_max = 50)
====================================================================================================
  chi(omega_min = 1/T) = 1.740637e-01, chi(omega_min = 2 pi/T) = 1.647378e-05, ratio 10566.1; the pure low-frequency estimate (2 pi)^3 = 248 holds only for omega_min T << 1
  local sensitivity d ln chi / d ln omega_min at 2 pi/T: -0.01; at 1/T: -3.36
  -> on an IR-divergent spectrum the reported chi is a function of the declared cutoff and must carry it.

